# Popular Visual Studio Code Key Combinations for Windows

Here are some of the most commonly used keyboard shortcuts in VS Code for Windows:

---

## **General Shortcuts**
- `Ctrl + N`: Create a new file.
- `Ctrl + O`: Open a file.
- `Ctrl + S`: Save the current file.
- `Ctrl + Shift + S`: Save all open files.
- `Ctrl + W`: Close the current tab.
- `Ctrl + ,`: Open VS Code settings.
- `Ctrl + Shift + P`: Open the **Command Palette** (universal command search).
- `Ctrl + K Ctrl + S`: Open keyboard shortcuts configuration.

---

## **Navigation & Tabs**
- `Ctrl + P`: Quick file search and open.
- `Ctrl + G`: Go to a specific line number.
- `Ctrl + Tab`: Switch between open tabs.
- `Ctrl + Shift + Tab`: Navigate tabs in reverse order.
- `Alt + ← / →`: Navigate backward/forward in editor history.

---

## **Editing**
- `Ctrl + C / Ctrl + X / Ctrl + V`: Copy, Cut, Paste.
- `Ctrl + Z / Ctrl + Y`: Undo/Redo.
- `Ctrl + D`: Select the next occurrence of the current word (multi-cursor).
- `Shift + Alt + ↑ / ↓`: Duplicate line(s) up/down.
- `Alt + ↑ / ↓`: Move line(s) up/down.
- `Ctrl + /`: Toggle line comment.
- `Shift + Alt + A`: Toggle block comment.
- `Ctrl + Space`: Trigger code suggestions (IntelliSense).

---

## **Multi-Cursor & Selection**
- `Alt + Click`: Add multiple cursors.
- `Ctrl + Alt + ↑ / ↓`: Add cursors above/below.
- `Ctrl + L`: Select the current line.
- `Ctrl + Shift + L`: Select all occurrences of the current selection.

---

## **Search & Replace**
- `Ctrl + F`: Find in the current file.
- `Ctrl + H`: Replace in the current file.
- `Ctrl + Shift + F`: Search across all files in the workspace.
- `Ctrl + Shift + H`: Replace across all files.

---

## **Code Formatting**
- `Shift + Alt + F`: Format the entire document.
- `Ctrl + K Ctrl + F`: Format the selected code.

---

## **Integrated Terminal**
- `` Ctrl + ` ``: Toggle the integrated terminal.
- `Ctrl + Shift + ` ``: Create a new terminal instance.

---

## **Debugging**
- `F5`: Start/continue debugging.
- `F9`: Toggle breakpoint.
- `F10`: Step over.
- `F11`: Step into.
- `Shift + F11`: Step out.

---

## **Extensions & Views**
- `Ctrl + B`: Toggle the sidebar visibility.
- `Ctrl + Shift + X`: Open the Extensions view.
- `Ctrl + Shift + E`: Open the Explorer view.
- `Ctrl + Shift + F`: Open the Search view.
- `Ctrl + Shift + G`: Open the Source Control (Git) view.

---

## **Split Editor**
- `Ctrl + \`: Split editor vertically.
- `Ctrl + 1 / 2 / 3`: Switch between editor groups.

---

> **Tip**: Customize shortcuts via `File > Preferences > Keyboard Shortcuts`.  
> Use `Ctrl + K Ctrl + R` to view all default keybindings in a browser.
